// Windows writes the NULL SID `S-1-0-0` when an event has no account for a SID
// field, and collectors that translate SIDs render it as `NULL SID`. Neither
// becomes an OCSF user, while genuine names, SIDs, machine accounts, and
// localized built-in accounts survive. Only SID fields lose these values: an
// account named `S-1-0-0` keeps its name. The events follow the documented 4624
// and 4625 layouts; all values are invented.
